From: Pharma360 QA Team
Subject: [PATCH 005/05] Remove backup-db.sh from PostgreSQL container startup
Date: 2026-11-01

This patch removes the backup-db.sh script from the PostgreSQL container's
initdb.d directory. The script requires dependencies (pg_dump, gzip, curl)
that aren't available in the postgres:15-alpine image and causes startup failures.

The backup script should be run separately via cron or a dedicated container.

---
 docker-compose.yml | 1 -
 1 file changed, 0 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docker-compose.yml b/docker-compose.yml
index abc1234..def5678 100644
--- a/docker-compose.yml
+++ b/docker-compose.yml
@@ -26,7 +26,6 @@ services:
     volumes:
       - pharma360-db-data:/var/lib/postgresql/data
       - ./scripts/init-db.sql:/docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/init-db.sql
-      - ./scripts/backup-db.sh:/docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/backup-db.sh
     ports:
       - "${POSTGRES_PORT:-5433}:5432"
     networks:
---
To apply this patch:
  cd /workspace/github__DuDuEZN__Pharma-360
  patch -p1 < patches/005-remove-backup-db-from-docker-compose.patch

OR manually apply:
  1. Edit docker-compose.yml
  2. Remove line 29:
     - ./scripts/backup-db.sh:/docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/backup-db.sh

Note: This change is already applied in the current repository state.
The backup script can be run manually or via a dedicated backup container.
